examples/sort.ck: 0 errors, 0 warnings; 18 obligations proved
-- exit 0
$ checkers frobnicate
-- stdout
-- stderr
checkers: unknown command `frobnicate`

checkers — the Checkers build tool

USAGE:
    checkers check|run|build|trust|stage|parse ...   run the compiler, `ckc` (see `ckc --help`)
    checkers fmt [--check] [PATH]...                 format .ck files (see `checkers fmt --help`)
    checkers fmt -                                   format standard input
    checkers --version

`ckc` is found through CKC, else next to `checkers`, else on PATH.
-- exit 2
$ checkers fmt --check tests/fmt/basics.ck tests/fmt/blanks.ck
-- stdout
tests/fmt/basics.ck
tests/fmt/blanks.ck
-- stderr
-- exit 1
$ checkers fmt --check --check
-- stdout
-- stderr
usage: checkers fmt [--check] [PATH]...
       checkers fmt -

Formats each .ck file under each PATH (default: the current directory) in place.
--check changes nothing: it lists the files that would change, and fails if
there are any. `-` formats standard input to standard output.
-- exit 2
